  "note": "Expected outputs worked out by hand from AP_MotorsMulticopter::output() and AP_MotorsMatrix (all values exact in binary32). Parameters make the chain linear and the gains 1: SPIN_MIN 0, SPIN_MAX 1, THST_EXPO 0 (thrust_to_actuator(t) = 0 + 1 * (lift_max * t * battery_scale) = t), BAT_VOLT_MAX 0 (lift_max 1, battery filter reset to 1), air density 1 (compensation_gain 1/1 * 1/1 = 1), BAT_CURR_MAX 0 (current limit returns 1), SAFE_TIME 0, IDLE_SEC 0, SPIN_ARM 0, slew off, PWM 1000..2000, dt 2^-6, SPOOL_TIME 2^-4 (spool step 0.25). Throttle 0.5 with filter cutoff 0 (alpha 1): filtered throttle 0.5 while armed; the slew detector never has two timestamps in its last two slots, so slope() returns 0 and the slew rate stays 0. Step 0: set_desired_spool_state runs before set_interlock(true), so the desired state is forced to SHUT_DOWN for this step; SHUT_DOWN: all limits set, ceiling 0, every thrust +0, actuators 0, PWM = pwm_min 1000 (armed, SAFE_DISARM 0). Step 1: desired THROTTLE_UNLIMITED, safe timer 0 >= SAFE_TIME 0, so SHUT_DOWN -> GROUND_IDLE; ground-idle actuator = spin_up_ratio * SPIN_MIN = 0, PWM 1000 + 1000 * 0. Steps 2-5: spin_up_ratio 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1; at 1 spin-up completes and the step sets the spool-up block (spoolup_block true at step 5). Step 6: the adapter clears the block before output(), so GROUND_IDLE -> SPOOLING_UP; the ceiling is still 0 this step (limits all set, thrust 0, actuator thrust_to_actuator(0) = 0). Step 7: SPOOLING_UP clears the limits, ceiling 0 + 0.25 < MIN(0.5, 1); throttle_thrust 0.5 clamped to 0.25 with limit.throttle_upper; throttle_avg_max 0.25, best = 0.25, rpy all 0, so thrust_rpyt_out = 0.25 on every motor, actuator 0.25, PWM 1250, throttle_out 0.25. Step 8: ceiling 0.5 >= MIN(0.5, 1) -> ceiling 1, THROTTLE_UNLIMITED; zero torque: every motor 0.5, PWM 1500, no limit flag. Step 9, pure roll 0.25: the normalized quad-X roll factors are (-0.49999997, 0.49999997, 0.49999997, -0.5) (cosf(radians(angle + 90)) for angles 45, -135, -45, 135 is -0.70710677, 0.70710677, 0.70710677, -0.70710683; normalise_rpy_factors divides by the largest magnitude), pitch (0.5, -0.5, 0.5, -0.5), yaw (0.5, 0.5, -0.5, -0.5). roll_thrust 0.25 gives rp = (-0.125 + 2^-27, 0.125 - 2^-27, 0.125 - 2^-27, -0.125); rpy_low -0.125, rpy_high 0.125 - 2^-27, rpy_scale 1, best = 0.125, thr_adj = 0.5 - 0.125 = 0.375 (not clipped: 0.375 < 1 - 0.25), base 0.5; 0.5 - 0.125 + 2^-27 rounds to 0.375 (quarter ulp) and 0.5 + 0.125 - 2^-27 rounds to 0.625: thrusts (0.375, 0.625, 0.625, 0.375), the quad-X sign pattern of a right roll (motors 2 and 3, the left side, up), actuators equal, PWM 1375, 1625, 1625, 1375, no limit flag; yaw allowed 0.75 > 0. Step 10: disarmed: the filter resets to 0, output_logic forces SHUT_DOWN, all limits set, ceiling 0, thrusts +0, actuators 0, PWM = pwm_min 1000 (SAFE_DISARM 0); the disarm saves MOT_THST_HOVER (cut: AP_Param::save is a no-op). Inputs added later (5: the `_seq` call-order fields and signals) are 0/false: fixed order, the steps are unchanged.",
